Package: upsil
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10)
Suggests: python3-tk
Description: UpsiL, a small language for AI scripts
 UpsiL has a Kotlin-like syntax and compiles to readable Python. Language
 models, document search and PyTorch networks are part of the language:
 [m] => "question" asks a model, -> json(shape) returns checked data,
 vector_store searches notes, model blocks are PyTorch modules and
 nn.fit trains them. On SOS it talks to the local model server
 (sos models serve), shows training progress in the bar and takes
 PyTorch from the project's environment (uv add torch; sos run uses it).
 .
 This package ships the "upsil" command (run, check, build, test, repl),
 syntax highlighting for Mousepad, GNOME Text Editor and Kate, the
 documentation and examples in /usr/share/doc/upsil, and a skill that
 teaches the assistant Jackson to write UpsiL.
